  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A projectile is projected with the velocity of $(3 \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}) \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s}$. The horizontal range of the projectile will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lpEMr",
      "text": "\r\n$1.2 \\mathrm{~m}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fBwQR",
      "text": "\r\n$2.4 \\mathrm{~m}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IKZpm",
      "text": "\r\n$3.6 \\mathrm{~m}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3IQJf",
      "text": "\r\n$4.5 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\mathbf{v}=3 \\hat{\\mathbf{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathbf{j}}$\r\n$$\r\n\\therefore \\quad v=|\\mathrm{v}|=\\sqrt{3^2+4^2} \\Rightarrow v=5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\r\n$$\r\nFrom figure,\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/S68DyZBu4WVIyvgm-kVZTbqOsJd6ueHWTqIkKHSEDW4.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n$\\sin \\theta=\\frac{4}{5}$ and $\\cos \\theta=\\frac{3}{5}$\r\n$\\because \\quad R=\\frac{v^2 \\sin 2 \\theta}{g}$\r\n$=\\frac{v^2 \\cdot 2 \\sin \\theta \\cdot \\cos \\theta}{g}$\r\n$=\\frac{5 \\times 5 \\times 2 \\times \\frac{4}{5} \\times \\frac{3}{5}}{10}=24 \\mathrm{~m}$",
    "image": null
  },
